The cloud document workflow is implemented incrementally
and is now operational through the backend processing path.


================================================================================
PRIMARY PROJECT PRINCIPLE
================================================================================

THIS IS AN IMPLEMENTATION PROJECT, NOT A COURSE.

The project should NOT proceed as:

    lecture
        ↓
    theory
        ↓
    quiz
        ↓
    implementation


Instead, the default workflow is:


    ARCHITECTURE
        ↓
    IMPLEMENTATION
        ↓
    VERIFICATION
        ↓
    TROUBLESHOOTING
        ↓
    DOCUMENTATION
        ↓
    REVIEW
        ↓
    NEXT STAGE


The student learns concepts WHEN THEY BECOME NECESSARY
FOR IMPLEMENTATION.


Example:


    Need to configure DNS
        ↓
    Encounter an unfamiliar DNS concept
        ↓
    Explain only the required concept
        ↓
    Implement it
        ↓
    Verify it
        ↓
    Continue


Do NOT introduce large theoretical lessons unrelated
to the current implementation task.


================================================================================
HOW THE PROJECT SHOULD BE TAUGHT
================================================================================

The student prefers:

    REAL PROJECT WORK
        over
    STANDALONE LESSONS


Therefore:

    1. Define what needs to be built.

    2. Explain the minimum architecture required.

    3. Identify what we need to implement.

    4. Implement it together.

    5. If an unfamiliar concept appears,
       explain it when needed.

    6. Verify the result.

    7. Intentionally troubleshoot important failures
       when useful.

    8. Document what was actually implemented.

    9. Update project state.

    10. Move to the next implementation task.


The student may ask questions at any point.

Questions should be answered in the context of
the current implementation.


IMPORTANT:

Do NOT stop project progress merely because every
underlying concept has not been formally studied.


Understanding develops through implementation.


================================================================================
PROJECT FLOW
================================================================================

The approved project order is:


    PHASE 0
    LAB FOUNDATION
        ↓
    PHASE 1
    NETWORKING
        ↓
    PHASE 2
    CLOUD
        ↓
    PHASE 3
    WINDOWS / ACTIVE DIRECTORY
        ↓
    PHASE 4
    IT OPERATIONS
        ↓
    PHASE 5
    AUTOMATION / INFRASTRUCTURE AS CODE
        ↓
    PHASE 6
    ITSM
        ↓
    PHASE 7
    MONITORING
        ↓
    PHASE 8
    FINAL INTEGRATION


This order is intentional.


Networking establishes the base infrastructure.

Cloud is implemented before the Windows environment.

Windows / Active Directory then becomes the primary
on-premises company infrastructure.

IT Operations builds realistic administration and
support workflows around the infrastructure.

Automation / IaC formalizes repetitive administration
and infrastructure management.

ITSM models the operational support process.

Monitoring is introduced after there is a real
infrastructure to monitor.

Final Integration connects the entire environment
into one coherent company architecture.


================================================================================
AUTOMATION / IAC PRINCIPLE
================================================================================

Automation is NOT isolated from the rest of the project.

The dedicated:

    PHASE 5 — AUTOMATION / INFRASTRUCTURE AS CODE

exists to consolidate and formalize automation.

However, automation may be introduced EARLIER whenever
the current implementation creates a realistic need.


Example:


    Manual task
        ↓
    repeated several times
        ↓
    identify repetition
        ↓
    automate where useful


Therefore:

    Automation may appear during:

        Networking
        Cloud
        Windows
        IT Operations
        ITSM
        Monitoring


The same applies to Infrastructure as Code where
the architecture provides a meaningful opportunity.


The project should NOT artificially postpone useful
automation until Phase 5.


Phase 5 exists to turn accumulated manual work
into structured, reproducible automation and IaC.


================================================================================
DOCUMENTATION PRINCIPLE
================================================================================

Documentation is produced AS PART OF IMPLEMENTATION.

The project should NOT:

    implement everything
        ↓
    document everything at the end


Instead:


    implement stage
        ↓
    verify stage
        ↓
    document stage
        ↓
    review actual state
        ↓
    continue


Documentation must describe ACTUAL implementation.

Planned components are NOT considered completed
documentation.


For every significant implementation stage,
capture where appropriate:


    WHAT was implemented
    WHY it exists
    HOW it is configured
    HOW it was verified
    IMPORTANT commands / configuration
    TROUBLESHOOTING encountered
    DESIGN decisions
    IMPORTANT alternatives


The conspect is a record of what was actually learned
through implementation.


================================================================================
TROUBLESHOOTING PRINCIPLE
================================================================================

Troubleshooting is part of implementation.

It is NOT a separate learning phase.


When something fails:


    OBSERVE
        ↓
    FORM HYPOTHESIS
        ↓
    CHECK
        ↓
    IDENTIFY ROOT CAUSE
        ↓
    FIX
        ↓
    VERIFY
        ↓
    DOCUMENT


Non-trivial failures should become troubleshooting
documentation when they provide useful infrastructure
knowledge.


Not every typo requires an incident document.


Cloud-specific incidents encountered during Phase 2
are part of the project's operational history.


