================================================================================
PHASE 2 — CLOUD INCIDENTS
================================================================================

INC-001
-------

Title:


    Floci State Loss / Persistence Misconfiguration


Summary:


    Floci cloud resources appeared to be lost after
    combining / changing Docker Compose configuration.


Investigation established that the new Compose
configuration was using a different / newly initialized
volume rather than binding the previously used Floci
state.


The existing cloud state was associated with the
previous storage configuration and was not being
presented to the new container.


Root cause:


    The Compose configuration referenced new storage
    rather than the existing Floci state volume.


Resolution:


    Identify the previously used persistent storage
    and bind the Floci deployment to the existing
    volume instead of initializing a new one.


Operational lesson:


    A Docker volume being present does not automatically
    mean that the application is using the correct volume.


    When changing Compose configurations:


        identify existing volumes
            ↓
        inspect their contents
            ↓
        identify which volume contains application state
            ↓
        explicitly bind the correct volume


    Persistence must be verified at the application level,
    not only at the Docker level.


Document:


    docs/incidents/INC-001-floci-state-loss.md


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
INC-002
-------

Title:


    Floci Lambda Execution Failure


Summary:


    Lambda invocation failed because Floci could not
    communicate with the Docker daemon from inside
    the Floci container.


Root cause:


    Floci Lambda execution requires Docker access.


Observed error:


    java.net.SocketException:
    No such file or directory


Investigation:


    Floci attempted to access:


        unix:///var/run/docker.sock


    but the Docker socket was not accessible.


Resolution:


    Mount the host Docker socket into the Floci container:


        /var/run/docker.sock
            →
        /var/run/docker.sock


Verification:


    [x] Docker socket visible inside Floci
    [x] Lambda container created
    [x] Lambda container started
    [x] Lambda invocation successful
    [x] SQS event source successfully invoked Lambda


Document:


    docs/incidents/INC-002-floci-lambda-exec-failure


