Important Phase 2 lessons:


    [x] Docker named-volume persistence must be verified
        against actual application state.

    [x] Changing Compose storage configuration can expose
        a different volume and make existing application
        state appear lost.

    [x] Floci Lambda execution requires Docker socket access.

    [x] Local AWS-compatible environments may not reproduce
        AWS authorization behavior exactly.

    [x] IAM policy design should remain aligned with the
        intended AWS architecture rather than emulator
        limitations.


